"description_full":"Gemini Space Station, Inc. operates a cryptocurrency platform in the United States and internationally. The company offers Gemini, a platform that enables users to trade, custody, and earn in a range of digital assets and offerings; Gemini ActiveTrader for advanced charting, multiple order types, and the ability to monitor and execute in multiple markets; and Gemini Derivatives to trade perpetual contracts with cross-collateralization for risk and capital management. It also provides Gemini Prediction for trading event contracts; custody solutions; and Gemini Credit Card for users to earn crypto rewards. The company serves institutional investors, including asset managers, hedge funds, proprietary trading firms, and corporations, as well as individual retail users. Gemini Space Station, Inc. was founded in 2014 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Tyler  Winklevoss | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 42 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 650 people. Revenue per employee of $276K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $131K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Gemini Space Station, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $311M market cap on $180M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -119% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $220M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 47% of revenue is silent dilution an